  "term": "diplacusis",
  "definition": "Diplacusis is a difference in how the two ears perceive the pitch of the same sound when each ear is heard separately. The source notes that this difference varies across people, may be as large as about a quarter-tone, and can also occur in connection with pathological conditions.",
